---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---
<BaseLayout title="About" description="Who this is and what this site is for.">
  <header class="page-head">
    <p class="eyebrow">About</p>
    <h1>Andrae Williams</h1>
    <p class="lede">AI · Software · Cyber · Risk · Systems</p>
  </header>
  <div class="prose">
    <p>
      This site is a technical second brain kept in public. It is where I work
      things out — what I am learning, what I am building, what broke, and what
      I would do differently.
    </p>
    <h2>What is here</h2>
    <p>
      Posts are organised by <a href="/topics/">topic</a> and, where they form a
      sequence, by <a href="/feed/">series</a>. The <a href="/lab/">lab</a> holds
      live experiments; <a href="/projects/">projects</a> holds things that
      actually shipped. <a href="/resources/">Resources</a> is the reference
      library I actually reach for.
    </p>
    <h2>How it is written</h2>
    <p>
      Every entry aims to do at least one of: learn, build, explain, test,
      analyse, visualise, reference, or connect. This is a growing map, not a
      publishing treadmill — so there is no schedule, and older entries get
      updated rather than replaced.
    </p>
    <h2>Provenance</h2>
    <p>
      Projects and lab entries record what was built by AI and which model wrote
      it. Posts are mine. That distinction is deliberate and it is visible on
      every entry that has one.
    </p>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
<style>
  .page-head { padding: var(--sp-6) 0 var(--sp-5); border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line); margin-bottom: var(--sp-5); }
  h1 { font-size: var(--step-3); margin: var(--sp-3) 0; }
  .lede { color: var(--text-1); font-family: var(--font-mono); letter-spacing: 0.08em; }
  .prose { max-width: 68ch; }
  .prose h2 { font-size: var(--step-1); margin-top: var(--sp-6); }
</style>
